::ALG2_U02_L02_GP01::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U02_L02_GP01<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.PF.4<br><br>Question:<br>What is the vertex of f(x) = (x - 4)<sup>2</sup> - 9? {
=(4, -9) #Correct. Vertex form gives (4, -9).
~(-4, -9) #The sign is reversed.
~(4, 9) #The k-value should be -9.
~(-9, 4) #Coordinates are reversed.
}

::ALG2_U02_L02_GP02::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U02_L02_GP02<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.PF.4<br><br>Question:<br>What is the axis of symmetry for f(x) = (x + 2)<sup>2</sup> + 5? {
~x = 2 #The sign is reversed.
~y = -2 #The axis is vertical.
=x = -2 #Correct. The vertex x-coordinate is -2.
~y = 5 #This is not the axis.
}

::ALG2_U02_L02_GP03::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U02_L02_GP03<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.PF.4<br><br>Question:<br>For h(t) = -16(t - 3)<sup>2</sup> + 144, what is the maximum height? {
~3 #This is the time.
=144 #Correct. The maximum output is 144.
~-16 #This is the leading factor.
~0 #The maximum is not 0.
}

::ALG2_U02_L02_GP04::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U02_L02_GP04<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.PF.4<br><br>Question:<br>If f(x) = x<sup>2</sup> - 6x + 8, what are the x-intercepts? {
~(-2, 0) and (-4, 0) #Signs are reversed.
~(0, 2) and (0, 4) #These are y-axis points.
~(6, 0) and (8, 0) #These are coefficients.
=(2, 0) and (4, 0) #Correct. Zeros are 2 and 4.
}

::ALG2_U02_L02_GP05::
Question ID:<br>ALG2_U02_L02_GP05<br><br>MLA Standard:<br>MLA.A2.PF.4<br><br>Question:<br>For a projectile that starts at t = 0 and lands at t = 5, what domain is meaningful? {
~all real numbers #Context restricts time.
=0 &le; t &le; 5 #Correct. Launch to landing.
~t &ge; 5 #This excludes the flight.
~t &le; 0 #This excludes most of the flight.
}

